  "keyTakeaways": [
    "Soybeans are almost the whole story: heading 1201 is 77% of this chapter's exports, and China and Mexico alone take 31%.",
    "China's 2025 pullback, not a new foreign tariff, explains most of the decline — its purchases fell 74% in 2025, then U.S. exports of this chapter were up 25% in the first seven months of 2026.",
    "Outside China, there is almost no tariff story: Mexico, Canada, the EU, Japan and Egypt all buy this chapter's goods duty-free or close to it.",
    "China's own September 2026 goodwill tariff list still excludes non-seed soybeans — the single biggest line in this chapter — so its extra 10% tariff stays in place even as other U.S. farm goods got relief."
  ],
